prompt.sdd.runner.repair.unbacked:
Your answer claims {count} scenario(s) were executed and no command of this stage backs them:
{scenarios}

The commands your sandbox ran in this stage (only these can back a claim; the app's own before you are context):
{commands}

Answer once more, whole, in the same form as before (summary, artifacts with the test plan, comment and scenarios), after one of these for each scenario: keep the evidence you looked at with SaveEvidence and cite the command that backs it; cite the command that backs it; say in `evidence` that it was only read; or that it did not run, with `result` as `not-run`. A scenario that still claims execution with nothing behind it is recorded as read by the app.

prompt.sdd.runner.repair.evidence:
Your answer concludes {count} scenario(s) with no evidence kept by this stage behind them:
{scenarios}

The evidence this stage has kept so far (only these ids exist):
{kept}

An id exists only once SaveEvidence hands it back: do not guess the next number. For each scenario, keep the result that backs it (the command's log or report, or a screenshot) from the output folder with SaveEvidence and cite in `evidenceIds` the id the tool returns, or cite one of the pieces above that backs it, or set `result` to `not-run` saying why. Answer once more, whole, in the same form as before (summary, artifacts with the test plan, comment and scenarios). A scenario still without evidence fails the stage.
